{"relation":"dlktk/discussion","args":{"id":"jivog-lisas","title":"Okta twin deepening — design decisions","subject":"q:resolve the seven open questions in PLAN-OKTA-DEEPEN.md and set the mocksys-feature vs okta-kit boundary","created_by":"chazu"},"source":"chazu","valid_start":1783347894}
{"relation":"dlktk/node","args":{"id":"rabal-farig","disc":"jivog-lisas","kind":"argument","text":"CONFIRMED against Okta's live integration test okta-sdk-dotnet GroupApiTests.cs:554-555 ('Idempotency - Unassign user not in group (should not throw)') — a non-member unassign returns 204, not 404. Success=204 confirmed at :528-530; 404 is only for a bad group/user id (OpenAPI ErrorResourceNotFound404). Bonus: :549-551 confirms assign is idempotent, validating the link verb. The earlier 'inferred' caveat is resolved.","author":"fidelity-bot"},"source":"fidelity-bot","valid_start":1783349030}
{"relation":"dlktk/node","args":{"id":"dufat-nilah","disc":"jivog-lisas","kind":"argument","text":"Masking with --ignore hides the WHOLE token, so conform can no longer diff claims — it would have silently hidden the aud/sub/scp errors the review just caught (M1/M2), defeating conform's purpose for this feature","author":"fidelity-bot"},"source":"fidelity-bot","valid_start":1783348010}
{"relation":"dlktk/node","args":{"id":"mavar-fihoz","disc":"jivog-lisas","kind":"argument","text":"A status==ACTIVE filter is a single list clause (filter=status eq ACTIVE), not a lifecycle state machine; it buys real fidelity cheaply without the out-of-scope lifecycle transitions","author":"fidelity-bot"},"source":"fidelity-bot","valid_start":1783347970}
{"relation":"dlktk/node","args":{"id":"matuv-kotiz","disc":"jivog-lisas","kind":"argument","text":"The twin is deliberately permissive elsewhere in the flow (no client_secret, no PKCE), so a status filter is inconsistent extra scope","author":"shipper-bot"},"source":"shipper-bot","valid_start":1783347970}
{"relation":"dlktk/node","args":{"id":"matuf-jipuj","disc":"jivog-lisas","kind":"argument","text":"Real Okta refuses to issue tokens for non-ACTIVE (STAGED/DEPROVISIONED) users; the default seed even ships carol=STAGED, so permissive auth is an observable divergence out of the box that could mask a bug in the code under test","author":"fidelity-bot"},"source":"fidelity-bot","valid_start":1783347970}
{"relation":"dlktk/node","args":{"id":"matoj-muzud","disc":"jivog-lisas","kind":"position","text":"No: permissive — any seeded/created user can authenticate (v1)","author":"shipper-bot"},"source":"shipper-bot","valid_start":1783347970}
{"relation":"dlktk/node","args":{"id":"matin-gitas","disc":"jivog-lisas","kind":"position","text":"Yes: only ACTIVE users appear in the picker and can be issued tokens (Okta-faithful)","author":"fidelity-bot"},"source":"fidelity-bot","valid_start":1783347970}
{"relation":"dlktk/node","args":{"id":"matat-paduv","disc":"jivog-lisas","kind":"issue","text":"Q7: restrict the account picker + token issuance to status==ACTIVE users?","author":"fidelity-bot"},"source":"fidelity-bot","valid_start":1783347970}
{"relation":"dlktk/node","args":{"id":"masom-dilak","disc":"jivog-lisas","kind":"argument","text":"The mock signing key is non-secret BY DESIGN (it signs fake tokens for a local twin) and is documented as such; --signing-key is opt-in, default stays ephemeral","author":"maint-bot"},"source":"maint-bot","valid_start":1783347970}
{"relation":"dlktk/node","args":{"id":"masir-jalud","disc":"jivog-lisas","kind":"argument","text":"A committed private key looks like a leaked secret","author":"sec-bot"},"source":"sec-bot","valid_start":1783347970}
{"relation":"dlktk/node","args":{"id":"masav-fuguk","disc":"jivog-lisas","kind":"argument","text":"Committed conform corpora and CI need a stable JWKS across regenerations; without a pin, every 'kit okta' re-mint produces a different kid/n and breaks a checked-in golden","author":"maint-bot"},"source":"maint-bot","valid_start":1783347970}
{"relation":"dlktk/node","args":{"id":"masaf-limib","disc":"jivog-lisas","kind":"position","text":"No: always random per invocation, no pin option","author":"shipper-bot"},"source":"shipper-bot","valid_start":1783347970}
{"relation":"dlktk/node","args":{"id":"maruj-nobav","disc":"jivog-lisas","kind":"position","text":"Yes: default random-per-invocation (stable within a contract), plus opt-in --signing-key FILE.pem for reproducibility","author":"maint-bot"},"source":"maint-bot","valid_start":1783347970}
{"relation":"dlktk/node","args":{"id":"maron-mojuh","disc":"jivog-lisas","kind":"issue","text":"Q6: offer --signing-key to pin the RSA key across kit invocations?","author":"maint-bot"},"source":"maint-bot","valid_start":1783347970}
{"relation":"dlktk/node","args":{"id":"marah-jubud","disc":"jivog-lisas","kind":"argument","text":"It is small (base64url-decode + JSON-parse + mask 4 volatile claims) and is a REUSABLE conform capability for any JWT-issuing twin; it lands ALONGSIDE feature 2, not before it, so it is not a blocker","author":"maint-bot"},"source":"maint-bot","valid_start":1783347970}
{"relation":"dlktk/node","args":{"id":"mapuj-kogig","disc":"jivog-lisas","kind":"argument","text":"A new normalizer is scope on the critical path and could block feature 2's ship","author":"shipper-bot"},"source":"shipper-bot","valid_start":1783347970}
{"relation":"dlktk/node","args":{"id":"mapin-tilis","disc":"jivog-lisas","kind":"position","text":"Build a minimal JWT-aware conform normalizer now (decode, drop sig/jti/iat/exp, diff claims), landing alongside feature 2","author":"maint-bot"},"source":"maint-bot","valid_start":1783347970}
{"relation":"dlktk/node","args":{"id":"mapar-jikah","disc":"jivog-lisas","kind":"position","text":"Ship feature 2 with documented --ignore of jti/access_token/id_token; build normalizer later","author":"shipper-bot"},"source":"shipper-bot","valid_start":1783347970}
{"relation":"dlktk/node","args":{"id":"manuz-vohak","disc":"jivog-lisas","kind":"issue","text":"Q5: for conform diffing of JWTs, build a JWT-aware normalizer now or ship with documented --ignore?","author":"maint-bot"},"source":"maint-bot","valid_start":1783347970}
{"relation":"dlktk/node","args":{"id":"manip-pibot","disc":"jivog-lisas","kind":"argument","text":"Forged/tampered-token testing is out of scope for v1 (a permissive mock with no client_secret/PKCE already); verifyJwt is a valuable v2 REUSABLE feature, deferred not rejected","author":"maint-bot"},"source":"maint-bot","valid_start":1783347970}
{"relation":"dlktk/node","args":{"id":"manat-dapub","disc":"jivog-lisas","kind":"argument","text":"A twin that ignores the JWT it issued can't catch a client that tampers claims or replays an expired token it forged","author":"sec-bot"},"source":"sec-bot","valid_start":1783347970}
{"relation":"dlktk/node","args":{"id":"manab-sanuk","disc":"jivog-lisas","kind":"argument","text":"verifyJwt adds a crypto-verify path + key handling for no v1 behavior gain: the bucket already carries the same ttl, so exp is enforced; and gating on the bucket is STRICTER than Okta (unknown-but-valid JWTs are rejected)","author":"shipper-bot"},"source":"shipper-bot","valid_start":1783347970}
{"relation":"dlktk/node","args":{"id":"mamuj-vohis","disc":"jivog-lisas","kind":"position","text":"Verify the presented JWT signature+exp in-twin (new verifyJwt verb)","author":"sec-bot"},"source":"sec-bot","valid_start":1783347970}
{"relation":"dlktk/node","args":{"id":"mamom-zanof","disc":"jivog-lisas","kind":"position","text":"v1: bucket is source-of-truth (JWT is for external consumers); bucket ttl already enforces exp","author":"shipper-bot"},"source":"shipper-bot","valid_start":1783347970}
{"relation":"dlktk/node","args":{"id":"mamir-gokik","disc":"jivog-lisas","kind":"issue","text":"Q4: at userinfo/CRUD, gate on the internal token bucket, or verify the presented JWT signature+exp?","author":"shipper-bot"},"source":"shipper-bot","valid_start":1783347970}
{"relation":"dlktk/node","args":{"id":"mamar-kitub","disc":"jivog-lisas","kind":"argument","text":"Evidence: Okta Go SDK GroupAPI.md documents UnassignUserFromGroup return as '(empty response body)' = 204. The non-member-\u003e204 idempotency is inferred from REST DELETE semantics + Okta's forgiving-delete pattern, NOT doc-confirmed; flag for a live check when credentials exist","author":"fidelity-bot"},"source":"fidelity-bot","valid_start":1783347970}
{"relation":"dlktk/node","args":{"id":"jofol-buzan","disc":"jivog-lisas","kind":"argument","text":"Okta's UnassignUserFromGroup is idempotent and returns 204 No Content regardless of prior membership; 404 would be an observable fidelity divergence","author":"fidelity-bot"},"source":"fidelity-bot","valid_start":1783347894}
{"relation":"dlktk/node","args":{"id":"jofir-bodal","disc":"jivog-lisas","kind":"position","text":"404 on non-member (reuse remove's miss path)","author":"shipper-bot"},"source":"shipper-bot","valid_start":1783347894}
{"relation":"dlktk/node","args":{"id":"jofav-guvod","disc":"jivog-lisas","kind":"position","text":"204 always (idempotent removal), matching Okta","author":"fidelity-bot"},"source":"fidelity-bot","valid_start":1783347894}
{"relation":"dlktk/node","args":{"id":"jofaf-bakof","disc":"jivog-lisas","kind":"issue","text":"Q3: DELETE group member on a non-member returns 204 or 404?","author":"fidelity-bot"},"source":"fidelity-bot","valid_start":1783347894}
{"relation":"dlktk/node","args":{"id":"jodob-pijut","disc":"jivog-lisas","kind":"argument","text":"That surface is paid once and is reusable: link/unlink/listJoin serve any many-to-many (GitHub team membership, Stripe customer-subscription), not just Okta","author":"maint-bot"},"source":"maint-bot","valid_start":1783347894}
{"relation":"dlktk/node","args":{"id":"jodig-vipit","disc":"jivog-lisas","kind":"argument","text":"More verbs = more compiler surface (validator whitelist + dispatch + docs per §1.4)","author":"shipper-bot"},"source":"shipper-bot","valid_start":1783347894}
{"relation":"dlktk/node","args":{"id":"jodal-safas","disc":"jivog-lisas","kind":"argument","text":"create always mints an id and returns a body; remove 404s on miss. link needs a composite path id + empty 204; unlink must 204 even on non-member. Flags would balloon both verbs with mode conditionals","author":"maint-bot"},"source":"maint-bot","valid_start":1783347894}
{"relation":"dlktk/node","args":{"id":"jobur-fatuv","disc":"jivog-lisas","kind":"position","text":"Flags on existing create/remove ({empty:true, idFrom:path})","author":"shipper-bot"},"source":"shipper-bot","valid_start":1783347894}
{"relation":"dlktk/node","args":{"id":"jobov-fazaj","disc":"jivog-lisas","kind":"position","text":"Distinct new terminal verbs link/unlink (+listJoin) — generic set/membership primitives","author":"maint-bot"},"source":"maint-bot","valid_start":1783347894}
